 "answer_text": "Found 1 disease record for Marfan syndrome: Marfan syndrome [13]. \n\nMarfan syndrome is an autosomal dominant multisystem connective tissue disease primarily caused by FBN1 mutations, producing a range of skeletal, ocular, and cardiovascular manifestations [1]. MedGen lists these clinical features: Aortic regurgitation [2], Arachnodactyly [3], Astigmatism [4], Ectopia lentis [5], Esotropia [6], Exotropia [7], Pes planus [8], Glaucoma [9], Congestive heart failure [10] and Hypertropia [11]. \n\nThe Ghent II Nosology criteria guide clinical identification of high-risk patients, and early diagnosis with treatment can prolong patient life span [12] [1]. \n\nDisease records found\n\nDisease name: Marfan syndrome [13]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Marfan syndrome [14]. Pubmed title: [Latest advances in the diagnosis and treatment of Marfan syndrome] [78]. Pubmed title: What Is Marfan Syndrome [80]. Pubmed title: Marfan syndrome [82]. Pubmed title: Marfan syndrome [84]. \n\nMedgen records found\n\nMedgen title: Marfan syndrome [15]. \n\nClinical features MedGen lists for Marfan syndrome\n\nMedgen clinical_features: Aortic regurgitation [2]. Medgen clinical_features: Arachnodactyly [3]. Medgen clinical_features: Astigmatism [4]. Medgen clinical_features: Ectopia lentis [5]. Medgen clinical_features: Esotropia [6]. Medgen clinical_features: Exotropia [7]. Medgen clinical_features: Pes planus [8]. Medgen clinical_features: Glaucoma [9]. Medgen clinical_features: Congestive heart failure [10]. Medgen clinical_features: Hypertropia [11]. Medgen clinical_features: Micrognathia [16]. Medgen clinical_features: Mitral regurgitation [17]. Medgen clinical_features: Mitral valve prolapse [18]. Medgen clinical_features: Myopia [19]. Medgen clinical_features: Pneumothorax [20]. Medgen clinical_features: Emphysema [21]. Medgen clinical_features: Retinal detachment [22]. Medgen clinical_features: Retrognathia [23]. Medgen clinical_features: Scoliosis [24]. M